@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: one Bubble Tea Program holds the terminal for a whole walk of forms — asks, a run's rows, hand-offs that lend the terminal out and dialogs over the card — with ui.Default held and every other program refused
' covers: internal/choiceui/session.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/session_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/session_term_test.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/tty_unix.go, internal/choiceui/tty_windows.go (openTerminal's guard, ttyFiles)
' covers: internal/choiceui/quit_gate.go (overlayDialog: the quit gate and Session.Dialog share it)
' covers: internal/choiceui/choiceui.go (formModel.ended; Selection and FieldValue read rows in place)
' covers: internal/choiceui/dialog_run.go (askDialog warns while a Session holds the terminal)
' covers: internal/ui/hold.go, internal/ui/hold_test.go
'   the plan this builds (§4, stage 3) .. scratchpad init-checklist-spec.md, §9.5 for what it measured
'   the card it hosts .................. _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml (THE CHECKLIST CARD)
'   the frame line ..................... _spec/internal/ui/step-lines.puml (THE HAND-OFF FRAME)
'   the quit gate and dialog overlay ... _spec/internal/choiceui/confirm-dialogs.puml
'   the library and its pins ........... _spec/internal/choiceui/tui-stack.puml
'   what the hold swaps ................ _spec/internal/ui/output-vocabulary.puml (HOLD)
'
' ── STATUS (2026-11-13, stage 3) ───────────────────────────────────────────
' BUILT, NOT USED. No caller outside the tests opens a Session yet. `proveo
' init` still runs one Program per page through Form.RunStep; stage 4 moves
' it onto one Session.
'
' ── WHY ONE PROGRAM PER WALK (D22, D29) ───────────────────────────────────
' A Program per page leaves the alternate screen between pages: the card
' flickers, and whatever printed between two Programs stays on the primary
' screen. One Program per walk leaves it only for a hand-off, so the
' scrollback holds frame lines and child output, nothing else.
' A second Program on the same terminal would race the walk for /dev/tty.
' openTerminal therefore refuses with ErrTerminalHeld while a Session is
' open, and so does a second OpenSession. RunStep, askDialog, the scope
' page, the check page and the filter list all go through openTerminal, so
' each fails loudly instead of racing. askDialog answers the safe way
' (asked=false) and warns "<dialog title> — not asked: a card holds the
' terminal"; the hold keeps that line until Close replays it. A driver on a
' Session asks through Session.Dialog instead (stage 4 moves init's glyph
' question there).
'
' ── THE API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   OpenSession() (*Session, error)     claims the terminal, opens /dev/tty,
'                                       holds ui.Default, starts the Program
'   Ask(f) (Outcome, error)             f at rest; Accepted leaves f up,
'                                       running, until the next Ask
'   Plan(labels)                        planned rows "·", other answers "–"
'                                       with their answer, "running i of m"
'   Status(label, mark, outcome)        one row; MarkRunning names the row
'                                       the key line counts, and after 2 s
'                                       its outcome gains " · 12s"
'   Hand(command, parts, run, outcome)  lends the terminal to run (below);
'                                       catches SIGINT from the call until
'                                       the card is back
'   Dialog(d) (int, error)              d over the dimmed card
'   Context()                           cancelled by ctrl+c while running
'                                       or after Enter, by a SIGINT during
'                                       Hand, by Close
'   Close() error                       Quit, wait, cancel, release the
'                                       hold, Replay it, close the tty,
'                                       free the claim
' A form Ask was given belongs to the Session until the next Ask. The model
' writes its rows (Plan, Status, the clock, a hand-off's outcome) on the
' event loop, so the driver reads answers from it and never writes them.
' The model writes only Kind, Mark and Outcome. Selection and FieldValue
' read each row in place (&f.Rows[i]) and touch only Label, Field,
' Selected, Options and Value, so a driver's read never races a write. A
' copy of the Row (range by value) would read all three written fields.
' Every call after the Program stopped returns ErrSessionEnded, wrapping the
' Program's own error when it had one.
'
' ── CTRL+C IN EACH STATE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   before the first Ask    cancels Context
'   a wizard page at rest   the form's quit gate; a second ctrl+c is Quit;
'                           Context stays live, the driver ends the walk
'   a lone form at rest     Cancelled
'   running (after Enter)   cancels Context; the key line reads "stopping
'                           after <row> …"; every other key is ignored
'   after Enter, before     cancels Context; the Plan that follows starts
'   the Plan                in "stopping after <row> …" (sessionModel.stopped)
'   after Back or Quit,     ignored: the page still shows its rest keys, and
'   before the next Ask     the driver puts the next page up or ends the walk
'   a Dialog                presses the dialog's ctrl+c button, and cancels
'                           Context (the run stops after its row)
'   a hand-off              cooked mode: SIGINT reaches proveo and the child.
'                           Hand catches it (signal.Notify), cancels Context
'                           and returns run's error as run gave it
' Hand calls signal.Notify before it sends the hand-off and signal.Stop
' after the reply. releaseTerminal puts the tty in cooked mode before the
' frame prints, and RestoreTerminal sets raw mode after run returns, so a
' Notify around run alone would leave both gaps open: a second Ctrl+C just
' after the child exits would kill proveo with the hold unreplayed. Raw
' mode turns Ctrl+C into a key, so a SIGINT from the tty arrives only while
' the hand-off has the terminal; handed reads the caught flag on handDone.
' Pinned by session_test.go: TestCtrlCFromEveryState,
' TestARunningFormTakesOnlyCtrlC; session_term_test.go:
' TestCtrlCWhileRunningCancelsTheContext,
' TestACtrlCDuringAHandOffStopsTheWalkAfterIt,
' TestACtrlCAsTheChildExitsStillStopsTheWalk.
'
' ── THE YIELD (§4.2), READ AND MEASURED ON bubbletea v2.1.1 ───────────────
' READ (exec.go, tea.go, cursed_renderer.go): tea.Exec runs on the event
' loop and blocks it. releaseTerminal cancels the input reader, waits up to
' 500 ms for its loop, stops the renderer (a last flush, then close: cursor
' to the bottom row, ESC[?1049l, cursor shown, bracketed paste off) and
' puts the tty's saved termios back (TIOCSETA / TCSETS: no input flush).
' RestoreTerminal sets raw mode again, starts a new reader, re-enters the
' alternate screen with a full repaint (enterAltScreen erases; `starting`
' defeats the no-change skip) and checks the size.
' handExec's Set* methods do nothing: run brings its own streams, as
' cmd/proveo's command() pins os.Stdin and os.Stderr.
' tea.Exec runs handExec.Run on the event loop, and handDone reaches the
' model only through `go p.Send` after RestoreTerminal. Run therefore puts
' the outcome on the card's row itself, so the first repaint shows it; the
' clock writes only a row still marked running, so a tick between the
' restore and handDone neither restores the running text nor counts the
' hand-off's time. handed writes the same outcome again and clears the
' running row.
' The frame and the outcome row draw plain (no colour) whenever ui.Default
' is plain: NO_COLOR, TERM=dumb, or no terminal on stderr, as handOff did
' through ui.Default before the Session.
' MEASURED 2026-11-13, darwin/arm64, a creack/pty slave at 80x24,
' TestAHandOffRunsARealChildAndReturnsToTheCard -count=30, 30/30 passed:
'   order on the pty: ESC[?1049l < frame < the child's echo and output <
'   the outcome row < ESC[?1049h
'   the frame showed 11-17 ms after Hand (kqueue cancelled the reader; the
'   500 ms fallback never ran)
'   two Asks and one hand-off: ESC[?1049h twice and ESC[?1049l twice
' MEASURED, a throwaway probe (10 runs per delay): keys typed 0 ms after
' Hand reached the card's reader in 10/10, so the child never saw them.
' At 1 ms, 3/10 reached the tty queue while it was still raw: the bytes
' survived, but a raw CR does not end a cooked line. From 3 ms on, 10/10
' reached the child whole.
' [Inference] Production opens /dev/tty, for which cancelreader uses
' select(2), not kqueue. The pty measured the kqueue path only.
'
' ── THE HOLD (D28) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' OpenSession calls ui.Hold() after the tty opens: ui.Default becomes a
' printer into memory with the same tier, plainness and section state. A
' live line draws nowhere while held. Close calls ui.Replay with what was
' held, after the Program left the alternate screen, so a missed capture
' shows rather than vanishes. Writes straight to os.Stdout or os.Stderr are
' not held; stage 4 captures each child that is not a hand-off.
'
' ── DECISIONS THAT DEPART FROM THE PLAN ───────────────────────────────────
' Hand takes the frame's command and parts, not a built line: only the
' Session knows the terminal's width, and FrameLine needs it.
' The outcome row reads the running row's label; Hand has no label of its
' own, because a hand-off is always a step of the plan.
' Dialog is opaque (Dialog{d dialog}); DrawsGlyphsDialog is the one stage 4
' needs. The dialog internals stay unexported.
'
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/session_test.go:
'   TestASessionKeepsOneProgramAcrossAsks
'   TestARunningFormTakesOnlyCtrlC
'   TestStepsUpdateTheirRowsWhileTheyRun
'   TestHandReleasesPrintsTheFrameAndRestores
'   TestTheCardComesBackWithTheHandOffsOutcome
'   TestAHandOffIsPlainWhenTheStreamIsPlain
'   TestAHandOffThatCannotTakeTheTerminalSaysSo
'   TestADialogDrawsOverTheDimmedCard
'   TestCtrlCFromEveryState
' Pinned by internal/choiceui/session_term_test.go (not on Windows):
'   TestAWalkOfPagesRunsOnOneSession
'   TestCtrlCWhileRunningCancelsTheContext
'   TestTheDriverReadsAnswersWhileTheRowsRun (-race)
'   TestANestedProgramIsRefusedWhileASessionHoldsTheTerminal
'   TestHeldLinesReplayAfterTheCard
'   TestACtrlCDuringAHandOffStopsTheWalkAfterIt
'   TestACtrlCAsTheChildExitsStillStopsTheWalk
'   TestAHandOffRunsARealChildAndReturnsToTheCard
' Pinned by internal/ui/hold_test.go: TestHeldOutputNeverReachesTheTerminal
title choiceui.Session — one Program per walk, and the hand-off that lends the terminal out

participant "the driver\n(init's walk, stage 4)" as DRV <<app>>
participant "Session" as SES <<app>>
participant "sessionModel\nthe event loop" as MOD <<app>>
participant "bubbletea\nexec / Restore" as TEA <<cloud>>
participant "handExec.Run" as HX <<app>>
participant "the terminal" as TTY <<host>>

DRV ARROW_MAIN SES : Ask(page) → Accepted
DRV ARROW_MAIN SES : Plan(rows), Status(row, ◐, what runs)
DRV ARROW_MAIN SES : Hand(command, parts, run, outcome)
SES ARROW_MAIN SES : signal.Notify(SIGINT)
SES ARROW_MAIN MOD : handMsg
MOD ARROW_MAIN TEA : tea.Exec(handExec, callback)
TEA ARROW_MAIN TTY : cancel reader, ESC[?1049l, cooked mode
TEA ARROW_MAIN HX : Run()
HX ARROW_MAIN TTY : blank row, "── command ── parts ──"
HX ARROW_MAIN TTY : run() — the child owns the terminal
HX ARROW_MAIN MOD : the row takes the outcome
HX ARROW_MAIN TTY : blank row, "  ✓ label  outcome"
TEA ARROW_MAIN TTY : raw mode, new reader, ESC[?1049h, repaint
TEA ARROW_MAIN MOD : handDone
MOD ARROW_MAIN SES : run's error; a caught SIGINT cancels Context
SES ARROW_MAIN SES : signal.Stop
SES ARROW_MAIN DRV : Hand returns run's error

note over MOD
  **Rows change on the event loop only.**
  Plan, Status and the clock write the form
  the View reads, so no write races a draw.
end note

note over HX
  **The frame and the row print on the primary**
  **screen.** The scrollback keeps what the child
  did between the two, after the card leaves.
end note

note over TEA
  **Keys typed in the first millisecond go to**
  **the card.** The reader read them before its
  cancel; from 3 ms on they reach the child.
end note

note over SES
  **One claim on the terminal.** openTerminal
  and a second Session refuse while it holds,
  so no program races the walk for /dev/tty.
end note
@enduml
